From: Win7 port restore
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] server.mjs: bundled-Python detection + offline wheel install

Applied to the node-port CLI/server bundle (dist/server.mjs, produced by
port-src/scripts/node-port/build.mjs). Makes Computer Use work fully offline
on Win7:
  - pythonBinPath(): honor basePythonOverride first
  - getBundledPythonDirsWin(): locate resources/runtime/python relative to
    the dist bundle (three fallback depths cover asar-unpacked layouts)
  - installRuntimeDependencies(): when a bundled wheels/ dir exists, run
    pip with --no-index --no-build-isolation --find-links (never touches
    the network); upstream path (pip upgrade + online install) preserved
  - ensureRuntimeFiles(): resolve requirements-win.txt / win_helper.py from
    multiple runtime roots; copy wheels next to the venv
  - venv bootstrap: fall back to the bundled python.exe when no system
    Python is present (Win7 ships none)
  - runSetup() venv fallback: also accept a user-configured custom python
    path that resolves to the bundled interpreter (embeddable python has
    no venv module; report the bundled fallback instead of failing setup)

Companion: patch-computer-use.py applies P1 (MIN_PYTHON_MINOR 9->8) and the
bundled-detection prologue; this diff is the full cumulative delta
(pre-CU backup -> shipped server.mjs).

